    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 21: bókpɔ̀nì</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bole_226">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bole</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bole_226_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>comme, ainsi, de la même façon ; (bole bole) quand même</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>like, thus, in the same way; (bole bole) all the same</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.2 Adverbs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bole</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bolinndo_227">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bolinndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bolin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bolinndo_227_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>blessure</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wound</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.3 Injure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 161: Bolinndo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bolinndo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme radicale bolin attestée (Gn 4,23 ; 1R 22,35).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bolinndo_228">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bolinndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bolinndo_228_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se blesser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hurt oneself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.3 Injure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Bolinndo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bolin</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de bolio.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bolio_229">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bolio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bolio_229_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>blesser</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wound, injure</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.3 Injure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 110: Bolio; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bolio/ boli; Childs 2000, p. 21: bòlìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Formes attestées dans la Bible : boli (EXO 21,25), bolin (GEN 4,23).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòlíŋndó_230">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòlíŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bòlíŋdáŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bòlíŋndó_230_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>grande harpe courbe à trois cordes</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>large curved three-stringed harp</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 21: bòlíŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bolle_231">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bolle</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="bolle_231_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>surtout</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>above all, especially</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.3 Very"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bolle</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Homographe de bolle « tête, chef » (forme radicale de bollen) ; sens à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bolle sɛllo_232">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bolle sɛllo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="bolle sɛllo_232_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>imam</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>imam</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.7 Religious organization"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 150: Bolle; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bolle</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit Bolle et Sèllo sur deux lignes, tous deux glosés « l'imam » : sans doute « chef (bolle) de la prière (sɛllo) », cf. Yondanɔɔ sɛllo « muezzin ». Dans la Bible, bolle « chef, tête » est attesté, mais sɛ̀llo y signifie « poix » (Ex 2,3). Le Lexique kissi–français, p. 7, glose bolle seul « l'imam ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bollen_233">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bollen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bóltan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bolle</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bollen_233_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tête ; sommet</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>head; top</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.1 Head"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>head; point, tip, edge, top</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 274 occurrences, first GEN.3.15; Keita 1979, p. 131: Bollen; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bollen; Childs 2000, p. 21: bòlléŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique kissi–français donne aussi bolten « la tête » (p. 7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòlló_234">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòlló</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bòltáŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bòlló_234_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pénis</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>penis</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.8 Internal organs"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.2 Sexual relations"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 21: bòlló</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bolofaa_235">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bolofaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="bolofaa_235_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>richesse(s)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wealth, riches</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.8.1 Have wealth"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 373 occurrences, first GEN.13.2</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bololan_236">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bololan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bolola</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bololan_236_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cou, gorge ; (kialu … bololan) égorger</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>neck, throat; (kialu … bololan) slaughter</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.2 Torso"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 79 occurrences, first GEN.22.10</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bololen_237">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bololen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="bololen_237_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gorge ; gourmand</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>throat; greedy (person)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.1 Head"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JER.2.25; Keita 1979, p. 131: Bololen; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bololen</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 7 : « la gorge ; gourmand ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boloo_238">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boloo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bolo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="boloo_238_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>navette (de tisserand)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>weaver's shuttle</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.1 Working with cloth"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>weaver's shuttle; anything of similar shape</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 159: Boloo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: boloo; Childs 2000, p. 22: bólóó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme radicale bolo dans la Bible (Jb 7,6).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bólòó_239">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bólòó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bólùá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bólòó_239_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce d'oiseau (qui s'attaque au riz)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>species of bird (raids rice)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 22: bólòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bólta_240">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bólta</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="bólta_240_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vallées, ravins</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>valleys, ravines</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2.1 Land"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>valley, base of a steep hill (singular bŏlló)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 21: bŏlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Forme radicale d'un pluriel en -lan (o bólta lan nin, Dt 2,36) ; la forme pleine se confondrait avec bóltan « têtes » (pluriel de bollen). Singulier non relevé.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòlɔ́ŋɔ̀ɔ́_241">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòlɔ́ŋɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bòllɔ́ŋùá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bòlɔ́ŋɔ̀ɔ́_241_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oiseau comestible de taille moyenne au chant mélodieux, difficile à voir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>edible medium-sized songbird, hard to see</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 21: bòlɔ́ŋɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bombo_242">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bombo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bombola</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bombo_242_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>plat, plaque ; (bombola kɔandaa) pelles à cendres</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pan, plate; (bombola kɔandaa) ash shovels</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.7 Container"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 10 occurrences, first 2KI.25.15</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>bombo icilinndo « plaque de fer » (Ez 4,3). À distinguer de l'idéophone bómbò (ɲum bómbò « disparaître », Ps 37,20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòmbòléŋ_243">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòmbòléŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="bòmbòléŋ_243_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>coupe de cheveux marquant un condamné ou un prisonnier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>haircut marking a convict or prisoner</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.4.3 Care for hair"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7.7 Punish"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 22: bòmbòléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bombosoo_244">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bombosoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bombosoo_244_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>variole</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>smallpox</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 161: Bombosoo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bonbosoo; Childs 2000, p. 22: bòmbòósòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bomndo_245">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bomndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bomndo_245_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oncle</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>uncle</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.9 Kinship"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>maternal uncle (mother's brother)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 134: Bomndo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bomndo; Childs 2000, p. 22: bòmndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bóndílló_246">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bóndílló</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="bóndílló_246_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>arbre à bois dur (charbon de bois)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hardwood tree (used for charcoal)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 22: bóndílló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Uapaca heudelotii (Childs, d'après Kew).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bondokpaa_247">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bondokpaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="bondokpaa_247_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>hémorroïdes, tumeurs</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>haemorrhoids, tumours</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first 1SA.5.6; Keita 1979, p. 161: Bondokpaa; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bondokpaa</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bondomaa_248">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bondomaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bondomalan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bondomala</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bondomaa_248_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>harpe, lyre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>harp, lyre</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 14 occurrences, first PSA.33.2</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. bondomanɔɔ « joueur de harpe ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bondomanɔɔ_249">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bondomanɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bondomanɔɔ_249_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>joueur de guitare, de harpe</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>guitar or harp player</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 145: Bondomanöö; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bondomanɔɔ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>bondomaa « harpe, lyre » est attesté (Ps 33,2).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bòndònɔ̀ɔ́_250">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bòndònɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bùndùá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bòndònɔ̀ɔ́_250_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>initiée (jeune fille de la société Bondo)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>female initiate (of the Bondo society)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.9 Culture"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.7 Religious organization"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 22: bòndònɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bondoo_251">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bondoo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="bondoo_251_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>société d'initiation des filles (Bondo, Sande) ; la case d'initiation</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>girls' initiation society (Bondo, Sande); the initiation house</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.9 Culture"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.7 Religious organization"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bondoo; Childs 2000, p. 22: bòndòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Confirmé au Nord par le Lexique kissi–français, p. 7 (« la clôture, l'endroit où les femmes passent la nuit pour l'excision »). Pluriel en kissi du Sud (Childs 2000) : bùndùláŋ.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bonio_252">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bonio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>bɔnio</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="bonio_252_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bol</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bowl</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.1 Household equipment"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.7 Container"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: bonio</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique écrit bonio et bɔnio (p. 7).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bonyii_253">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bonyii</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>bonyun</text></form></field>
    <sense id="bonyii_253_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jarre, cruche, récipient</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>jar, pitcher, vessel</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.7 Container"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 24 occurrences, first GEN.24.14</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boo_254">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="boo_254_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>coque, écorce, peau de fruit ; fourreau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shell, bark, peel; sheath</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 14 occurrences, first JOS.5.13; Keita 1979, p. 139: Boo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: boo; Childs 2000, p. 23: bòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la Bible, le fourreau de l'épée (1SA.17.51, 1CH.21.27).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boo tɛɛngaa_255">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boo tɛɛngaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="boo tɛɛngaa_255_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pagaie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>paddle</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.4 Travel"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7 Tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 159: Boo tèèngaa; Lexique kissi–français, p. 7: boo tɛɛngaa</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>tɛɛngaa « ramer » est attesté (vanaa tɛɛngaa ladɛ̀ndɛ̀a « les rameurs », Ez 27,8) ; dans la Bible, boo signifie « fourreau » (1 S 17,51).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="booluu_256">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>booluu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="booluu_256_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>blesser, frapper (à plusieurs reprises) ; inciser (le corps)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wound, strike (repeatedly); cut (the body)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.3 Injure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first LEV.19.28; Childs 2000, p. 23: bòòlùùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dérivé intensif de bolio « blesser ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boolɔnndo_257">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boolɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>boolɔnndan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>boolɔnnda</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="boolɔnndo_257_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>blessure, plaie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wound, sore</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.3 Injure"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 1KI.18.28; Childs 2000, p. 23: bòòlɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boondei_258">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boondei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>boondon</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>boondii</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>boondun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="boondei_258_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>articulation, jointure ; gond ; bouton (du chandelier) ; moment, époque</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>joint, socket; hinge; knob (of the lampstand); time, season</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.6 Bone, joint"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.1 Period of time"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>joint, knuckle, ankle</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 23: bòòndéí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>boondii ken « en ce temps-là » (Gn 6,4) ; a boondei he ɲinasiaŋ « l'an prochain à cette époque » (Gn 18,10) ; boondon « boutons » du chandelier (Ex 25,31).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="boosei_259">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>boosei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="boosei_259_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sorte d'instrument de musique (calebasse)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>a musical instrument (gourd instrument)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>gourd from a thorny tree; a gourd instrument that is blown or shaken</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first DAN.3.5; Childs 2000, p. 24: bòòsèí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dans la liste des instruments de l'orchestre de Nabuchodonosor (DAN.3.5, 3.7, 3.10, 3.15).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="booson_260">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>booson</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="booson_260_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>plantes épineuses, chardons</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>thorny plants, thistles</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.2 Bush, shrub"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>a thorny tree whose gourds are used as containers and instruments</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first JER.12.13; Childs 2000, p. 24: bòòsòó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel ; yɔɔn booson « épines et chardons » (JER.12.13, HEB.6.8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="bóóŋbóóŋndó_261">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>bóóŋbóóŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
