    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 38: cálŋcóŋjàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cám-càm_450">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cám-càm</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cám-càm_450_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tiède</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lukewarm</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.4 Hot"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 38: cám-càm</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cámbúéíyó_451">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cámbúéíyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cámbúéíyó_451_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>robe longue</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>long dress</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3 Clothing"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 38: cámbúéíyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Emprunt au mende jambueiyo.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="camndo_452">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>camndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="camndo_452_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>magie</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>magic</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.4 Miracle, supernatural power"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 150: Tyamndo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 8: camndo</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="can_453">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>can</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>cannin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="can_453_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se lever, partir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>get up, set out</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1.1 Stand"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>get up, arise; also grow, grow up</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 603 occurrences, first GEN.2.8; Childs 2000, p. 38: càŋɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>can-ndo « l'est » (où le soleil se lève).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="candɔɔ_454">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>candɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>candu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="candɔɔ_454_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>louer, honorer, estimer ; louange</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>praise, honour, esteem; praise</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.5.6 Status"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 20 occurrences, first JOB.29.11; Childs 2000, p. 38: càndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>O candu « il loue » (Gn 29,35, explication du nom de Juda).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="canyɛi_455">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>canyɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="canyɛi_455_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>amitié ; bonté, alliance</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>friendship; kindness, alliance</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.1.1 Friend"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>friendship; friend, lover</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 26 occurrences, first GEN.50.21; Keita 1979, p. 148: Tyaanyèi; Lexique kissi–français, p. 8: canyɛi; Childs 2000, p. 39: càɲèí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a caando « ami », pluriel caanda. La Bible écrit canyɛi (amitié, bonté, alliance). Le Lexique kissi–français donne aussi caaɲɛi « l'amitié » (p. 8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="capo_456">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>capo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="capo_456_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>beaucoup (adverbe de quantité)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>much, a lot (adverb of quantity)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 117: tyapo; Childs 2000, p. 39: cápò</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita, adverbes de quantité : Faya yöngu ndu maalon tyapo « Faya lui a donné beaucoup de riz ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="càúwó_457">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>càúwó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>càúwé</text></form></field>
    <sense id="càúwó_457_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>arbre des lieux humides et rives (fruit comestible bouilli longtemps)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tree of damp places and riverbanks (fruit edible after long boiling)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 39: càúwó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cawvo_458">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cawvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>caw</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="cawvo_458_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce d'arbre (son fruit : caw)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind of tree (its fruit: caw)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 9: cawvo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique ne précise pas l'arbre.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="càŋgàbìnèìyó_459">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>càŋgàbìnèìyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="càŋgàbìnèìyó_459_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>grande cuillère de cuisine à long manche</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>long-handled cooking spoon</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.1 Household equipment"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 38: càŋgàbìnèìyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="càŋgúlló_460">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>càŋgúlló</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="càŋgúlló_460_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce de poisson-chat, petit et trapu</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>species of catfish, small and thick</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 38: càŋgúlló</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="caŋnda_461">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>caŋnda</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="caŋnda_461_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>hanche, reins</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hip, loins</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.2 Torso"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>waist, lower belly</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 19 occurrences, first GEN.18.20; Keita 1979, p. 132: Tyannda; Lexique kissi–français, p. 8: cannda; Childs 2000, p. 39: càŋndá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Homographe : caŋnda « clameur, plainte » (Gn 18,20 ; Nb 14,27).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="caŋndo_462">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>caŋndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>caŋ</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ceŋ</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>caŋnin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ceŋnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="caŋndo_462_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pleurer ; pleurs ; hurler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>weep, cry ; weep, cry; weeping; wail</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>cry, weep, whine</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 123 occurrences, first GEN.21.16; Keita 1979, p. 115: Tyanndo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 8: canndo/ can, cen; Childs 2000, p. 39: càŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita écrit tyanndo ; la Bible écrit caŋndo (GEN 21,16). ceŋ, ceŋnin : radical négatif (GEN 43,31 ; MAT 11,17). Le Lexique kissi–français écrit canndo/ can, cen « pleurer, hurler » et canndo « les pleurs » (p. 8).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cécéŋ-_463">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cécéŋ-</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cécéŋ-_463_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>jeune (pour un adulte)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>young (of an adult)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.4 Stage of life"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 39: cécéŋ-</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cédé_464">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cédé</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cédé_464_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>piqûre vive (épine, aiguille)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sharp prick (thorn, needle)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 41: cédé</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ceendo_465">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ceendo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ceendo_465_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>monde, terre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>world, earth</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.2 World"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 375 occurrences, first GEN.1</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cèkècékáá_466">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cèkècékáá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cèkècékáá_466_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>rincer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rinse</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.6 Cleaning"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 41: cèkècékáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="celen_467">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>celen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="celen_467_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Determiner"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>autre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>other, another</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.5 Type, kind"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 783 occurrences, first GEN.4.25; Lexique kissi–français, p. 9: celen; Childs 2000, p. 39: cělèŋ-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Aussi Lexique kissi–français, p. 40 : « o celen ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="celianndo_468">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>celianndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>celian</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="celianndo_468_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>réussir à sauver ou à faire quelque chose</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>manage to save or do something</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.1.2 Do"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 9: celianndo/ celian</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Variante cerianndo (p. 9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cellen_469">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cellen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="cellen_469_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>plante lisse et fine (espèce)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>a smooth, slender plant</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 9: cellen</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="celullo_470">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>celullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>celul</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>celulaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="celullo_470_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>être gras, épais ; (celulaa) gras, engraissé</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be fat, thick; (celulaa) fat, fattened</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2 Big"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.3 Animal life cycle"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first JDG.3.17; Lexique kissi–français, p. 9: celullo/ celul; Childs 2000, p. 40: cèlùlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>naw téndé celulaa « veau gras » (1 S 28,24). Le Lexique kissi–français donne aussi cerullo/ cerul (p. 9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cénéwéíyó_471">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cénéwéíyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cénéwéíyó_471_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>luciole ; briquet, électricité, lumière vive, lanterne</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>firefly; cigarette lighter, electricity, bright light, lantern</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 41: cénéwéíyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="céŋ_472">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>céŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="céŋ_472_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>en douceur, régulièrement (animal entrant dans un trou ou en sortant)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>smoothly, evenly (of an animal entering or leaving a hole)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 40: céŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cèŋgéí_473">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgéí</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgóŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="cèŋgéí_473_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ergot pointu près de la queue de la poule (empêche l'accouplement) ; clitoris ; barbillons</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pin-like part near a hen's tail (said to prevent mating); clitoris; wattles</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.8 Internal organs"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 40: cèŋgéí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cèŋgímèìyó_474">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgímèìyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cèŋgímèìyó_474_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce de banane</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>species of banana</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 40: cèŋgímèìyó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Emprunt au mende jèmíŋàí.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cèŋgìó_475">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgìó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgìléŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="cèŋgìó_475_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>herbe à éléphant (savanes, plaines inondables ; remède pour l'oreille)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>elephant grass (savannas, floodplains; used for ear problems)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 42: cèŋgìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pennisetum purpureum (Childs).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cèŋgòó_476">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgòó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgèí</text></form></field>
    <sense id="cèŋgòó_476_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cœur du bois (partie dure, imputrescible)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>heartwood (hard, rot-resistant part)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.5 Parts of a plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 40: cèŋgòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cèŋgòó_477">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgòó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋgùá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="cèŋgòó_477_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>témoin du versement de la dot</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>witness to the payment of the bride price</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.1 Marriage"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7 Law"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 40: cèŋgòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="céŋndó_478">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>céŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="céŋndó_478_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>marteau de forgeron (servant aussi pour les remèdes)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>blacksmith's hammer (also used for preparing medicines)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.2 Working with minerals"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.2 Pounding tool"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 42: céŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cèŋùlló_479">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cèŋùlló</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cèŋùlló_479_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire claquer les lèvres (baiser pour amuser un bébé)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>smack one's lips (kissing noise to amuse a baby)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.7 Play, fun"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 42: cèŋùlló</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cí_480">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cí</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cí_480_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>complètement brûlé</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>badly burnt</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 42: cí</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cica_481">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cica</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="cica_481_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sauter ; s'élancer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>jump, leap</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first HAB.1.10; Childs 2000, p. 42: cìcàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>a cica lekɔɔli « ils s'élancent dessus (pour prendre les villes) » (HAB.1.10). Seule occurrence, sens à confirmer.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cícìŋ_482">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cícìŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cícìŋ_482_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>bruit d'une personne qui retombe après un saut</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>sound of landing after a jump</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 42: cícìŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciee-piɔ́m_483">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciee-piɔ́m</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ciee-piɔ́m_483_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>séjour des morts, pays des ancêtres</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>abode of the dead, land of the ancestors</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.6 Heaven, hell"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.6.6 Die"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>town of the dead</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 134 occurrences, first GEN.15.15; Childs 2000, p. 43: cíéé-pìɔ̀mndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De ciee « ville » et piɔ́m- « mort ». diam vanaa ndɔa ciee-piɔ́m « être réuni aux siens (mourir) » (GEN.25.8, JDG.2.10).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cieei_484">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cieei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="cieei_484_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>accident grave</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>serious accident</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4.2 Trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 9: cieei</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ciei_485">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ciei</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="i"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ciei_485_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>mortier ; mortier ; meule</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mortar; mortar; millstone</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.7.2 Pounding tool"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.1 Household equipment"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first NUM.11.8; Keita 1979, p. 160: Tyiei; Lexique kissi–français, p. 9: ciei; Childs 2000, p. 43: cìéí</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>cu ndu o ciei nin « le piler au mortier » (NUM.11.8) ; vanin cúo o ciei « moudre à la meule » (MAT.24.41) ; pow ... maa ciei « pierre comme une meule » (REV.18.21). Le Lexique kissi–français donne aussi cee « le mortier » (p. 9).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cìèì-dèndɔ̀ɔ́_486">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>cìèì-dèndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="cìèì-dèndɔ̀ɔ́_486_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>maison à pignon</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>house with a gable roof</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.5.1 Building"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 44: cìèì-dèndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="cìèì-kíkílló_487">
