      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.6.1 Working with cloth"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 206: kpàsàá kpàsàláŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kpasamaa_1819">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kpasamaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kpasamaa_1819_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>sorte de gale</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind of skin disease</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first DEU.28.22; Keita 1979, p. 161: Kpasamaa; Lexique kissi–français, p. 28: kpasamaa</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kpasan_1820">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kpasan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kpasan_1820_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ergots (du coq) ; pattes (sauteuses) des sauterelles</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spurs (of a rooster); (jumping) legs of locusts</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.2 Parts of an animal"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spur of a cock; extra finger; stiff tip of a boa's tail</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first LEV.11.20; Childs 2000, p. 206: kpàsèí kpàsǎŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel. kambalaa nɔ kan bɔɔlan a kpasan-nda « les insectes ailés qui ont des pattes (pour sauter) » (LEV.11.21) ; kongil nɔ nin kpasan-ndo « le coq aux ergots » (PRO.30.31).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kpasua_1821">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>kpasua</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="kpasua_1821_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vigoureux, robuste (jeunes gens)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>vigorous, sturdy (young men)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.4.1 Strong"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>big, large; enough; normal-sized</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first ISA.40.30; Childs 2000, p. 206: kpású-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Poambɔa kpasua sanga ma vi diallon « les jeunes gens vigoureux se fatiguent » (ISA.40.30). Une seule occurrence ; sens déduit du contexte.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="kpasukpasu_1822">
