  <entry id="seemaa_3461">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>seemaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>seema</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="seemaa_3461_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>folie, sottise ; (seema) être fou, devenir fou</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>madness, folly; (seema) be mad, go mad</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.1.2 Mental state"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>to act crazy (verb)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first PRO.17.12; Keita 1979, p. 162: Seemaa; Lexique kissi–français, p. 47: seemaa; Childs 2000, p. 323: sèèmàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 47 : seema « fou, devenir fou » (cf. JHN.10.20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="seemiaa_3462">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>seemiaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>seemiaanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="seemiaa_3462_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faire errer, égarer ; affoler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>make wander, lead astray; strike with panic</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.1.2 Mental state"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>act crazy (plural)</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 2SA.15.20; Childs 2000, p. 323: sèèmìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>i seemiaanin soa « je frapperai d'affolement les chevaux » (ZEC.12.4) ; mì kɔɛ vɛlɛ hau seemiaa a nɔm? « te ferais-je errer avec nous ? » (2SA.15.20) ; naa malɔɔ seemiaamì (ISA.63.17).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="seemɛi_3463">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>seemɛi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>seemɛiya</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>seemɛiyo</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>seemɛilan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="seemɛi_3463_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>fou, insensé ; (vana seemɛi) un fou</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mad, insane, foolish; (vana seemɛi) madman</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.1.2 Mental state"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>crazy, insane</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 8 occurrences, first 1SA.21.14; Lexique kissi–français, p. 47: semiyɛiyo; Childs 2000, p. 323: sèèméí-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>De seemaa « folie ». maa vana seemɛi « comme un fou » (1SA.21.14, 2KI.9.20) ; vanaa seemɛiya (1SA.21.16) ; vana seemɛiyo (ECC.10.14) ; nààla seemɛilan « la folie » (DEU.28.28) ; O seema « il est fou » (JHN.10.20).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="seenguuvo_3464">
