    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 337: sìɔ̀ùwé</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɔw_3598">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔw</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="siɔw_3598_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pourrir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>rot</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.4.1 Dead things"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 116: Siöw; Lexique kissi–français, p. 45: [s]a</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a siɔu, siɔ « (le jour) se lever » (JDG 19,26), sens différent. Lexique kissi–français, p. 45 : [s]a (rad) « pourrir » (lecture incertaine). Aussi Lexique kissi–français, p. 50 : « siɔu/ siɔ, sɛ, sia, si ». Lexique kissi–français, p. 50 : siɔu/ siɔ, sɛ, sia, si « pourrir ». Homographe de siɔu « poindre (le jour) ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɔŋio_3599">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔŋio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔŋ</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔŋi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔŋnin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔŋinin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔŋnun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siɔŋio_3599_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'user, s'abîmer ; user, ronger</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wear out, waste away; wear down, consume</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9 Break, wear out"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>age, get old</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JOB.16.9; Childs 2000, p. 336: sìɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>volɔɔla niaa la siɔŋ te « vos vêtements ne se sont pas usés » (Dt 8,4) ; siɔŋi « user, ronger » (Ps 39,12).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɔ́ŋndo_3600">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔ́ŋndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>sɛŋ</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siɔ́ŋndo_3600_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>dépecer, découper (une bête abattue) ; écorcher</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>butcher, cut up (a slaughtered animal); flay</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.3 Animal husbandry"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>butcher, slaughter</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first 2CH.35.11; Childs 2000, p. 336: sìɔ́ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>leviia nda va cɔlua sálàá siɔ́ŋndo « les lévites dépeçaient les bêtes » (2CH.35.11) ; a sɛŋ saa kóndó kon, a diw ndu kundalan « tu découperas le bélier en morceaux » (EXO.29.17) ; mà sɛŋ ndu (1KI.18.23).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɔ̀ɔ́_3601">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔ̀ɔ́lan</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔ̀ɔ́la</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siɔ̀ɔ́_3601_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>palmier</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>palm tree</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first LEV.11.14</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>siɔ̀ɔ́la vawlan « palmes, branches de palmier » (Lv 23,40).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɔɔ_3602">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="siɔɔ_3602_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>désherber autour des plantes (sans tout couper) ; nettoyer le chemin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>weed, clear the brush around plants; clear a path</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.4 Tend a field"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 50: siɔɔ; Childs 2000, p. 336: sìɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Confirmé au Nord par le Lexique kissi–français, p. 50 : siɔɔ « nettoyer le chemin ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sìɔ́ɔ́_3603">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sìɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sìɔ́ɔ́_3603_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>calebasse à graines, hochet (sasa, joué par les femmes)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>gourd rattle with seeds (sasa, played by women)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 336: sìɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="síɔ́ɔ́_3604">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>síɔ́ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="síɔ́ɔ́_3604_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>savon</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>soap</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.6.2 Bathe"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 337: síɔ́ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="sìɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ̀ɔ́_3605">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>sìɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="sìɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ̀ɔ́_3605_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>oiseau tisserand (au long nid)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>weaver bird (builds a long nest)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 337: sìɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɔɔndaa_3606">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔɔndaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɔɔnda</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siɔɔndaa_3606_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>chuchoter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>whisper</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 113: Siööndaa; Lexique kissi–français, p. 50: siɔɔndaa/ siɔɔnda</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="síɛ́kísíɛ́kíó_3607">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>síɛ́kísíɛ́kíó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="síɛ́kísíɛ́kíó_3607_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>insecte (genre abeille) qui fait du bruit en hochant la tête</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>bee-like insect that makes a noise by nodding its head</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 331: síɛ́kísíɛ́kíó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɛlaa_3608">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛlaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛla</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛlanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siɛlaa_3608_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>trébucher, glisser, chanceler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stumble, slip, totter</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>slip; also change the topic; dance</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first PSA.55.23; Lexique kissi–français, p. 48: sɛlaa/ sɛla; Childs 2000, p. 331: sìɛ̀làá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 48 : écrit sɛlaa/ sɛla.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɛlɛiyo_3609">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛlɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="siɛlɛiyo_3609_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>paresseux ; paresse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>lazy; laziness</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.1.1 Personality"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 23 occurrences, first JDG.18.9; Childs 2000, p. 331: sìèlɛ́í-</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɛmbulan_3610">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛmbulan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="lan"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛmbula</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siɛmbulan_3610_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>honte, opprobre</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shame, disgrace</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.4.2 Trouble"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>shame; shyness, bashfulness</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 233 occurrences, first GEN.30.23; Lexique kissi–français, p. 48: sɛnburan; Childs 2000, p. 336: sìɔ́mbúlɛ́ŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 48 : écrit sɛnburan.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɛmbullo_3611">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛmbullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛmbullon</text></form></field>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛmbulle</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="siɛmbullo_3611_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ronce, buisson épineux</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>brier, thorn bush</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.2 Bush, shrub"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>the fern tree (thorny) and its flowers</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first MAT.7.16; Childs 2000, p. 336: sìɔ̀mbúllɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>hɛɛnndon a siɛmbulle « épines et ronces » (Es 7,23).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="siɛndi_3612">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>siɛndi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="siɛndi_3612_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tendre (la main)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stretch out (the hand)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.3 Limb"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 63 occurrences, first GEN.8.9</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="síɛ́ndìíyáŋ_3613">
