      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 400: yáwèlè-yáwèlè</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yáwlen_4630">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yáwlen</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="len"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yáwlen_4630_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ceinture</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>belt, sash</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3.6 Parts of clothing"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 27 occurrences, first EXO.12.11; Keita 1979, p. 145: Yawlen; Lexique kissi–français, p. 64: yawlen; Childs 2000, p. 399: yàúléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yawnun_4631">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yawnun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="yawnun_4631_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cuire, être cuit (bouilli)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>be cooked, be boiled</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>be cooked, get hot, cook by itself</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first LEV.6.21; Childs 2000, p. 399: yàùnɔ̌ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de yawvo « cuire ». Te visin mun yawnun pɛ o kpɛɛnɛi « si la viande a cuit dans un pot » (LEV.6.21).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yáwvo_4632">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yáwvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yáw</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yáwvo_4632_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>peau</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>skin</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.4 Skin"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>skin, hide; paper, book; learning</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 25 occurrences, first GEN.25.29; Keita 1979, p. 133: Yawvo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 64: yawvo; Childs 2000, p. 399: yàúwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible écrit en général yáwvo dans ce sens ; yawvo sans ton y désigne aussi la cuisson, la préparation du repas (Gn 25,29).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yawvo_4633">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yawvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>yaw</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="yawvo_4633_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>cuire, préparer (la cuisine)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cook</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 25 occurrences, first GEN.25.29; Keita 1979, p. 115: Yawvo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 64: yawvo/ yaw, yew; Childs 2000, p. 399: yàùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen yawnun « cuire, être cuit » (LEV 6,21). Lexique kissi–français, p. 64 : radicaux yaw, yew.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="yáyâŋndó_4634">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>yáyâŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
