      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind of plant</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 274: ɲǎnìkpɔ́léŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲánndávàà_5033">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲánndávàà</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲánndávàà_5033_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>enfer, géhenne ; perdition (kɔɛ o ɲánndávàà « périr »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>hell, Gehenna; perdition (kɔɛ o ɲánndávàà 'perish')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.6 Heaven, hell"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 23 occurrences, first MAT.5.22</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲasɔɔ_5034">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲasɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲasɔɔ_5034_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>gratter, égratigner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scratch</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.5 Rub"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>scratch, make marks</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first DAN.6.24; Keita 1979, p. 114: Nyasöö; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲasɔɔ/ ɲasu, ɲesu; Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲàsɔ̀ɔ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Une occurrence (DAN 6,24, les lions). Le Lexique kissi–français donne aussi : ɲasu, ɲesu.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲasɔɔnndo_5035">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲasɔɔnndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲasun</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲesun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲasɔɔnndo_5035_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se gratter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>scratch oneself</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.7.5 Rub"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 114: Nyasöönndo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲasɔɔnndo/ ɲasun, ɲesun</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Moyen de ɲasɔɔ. Lexique kissi–français, p. 39 : aussi ɲɛsonndo « se gratter ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲavɛiyo_5036">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲavɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲavɛi</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲavɛiya</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲavɛyaa</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲavɛiyo_5036_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>maigre, chétif</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>thin, lean, gaunt</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.1 Small"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.4.2 Weak"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>thin, dry</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 2 occurrences, first EZK.34.20; Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲàwéí-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>navaa … ɲavɛyaa « les vaches maigres » (GEN.41.4). Cf. ɲawvo « maigrir ». Correspondance w ~ v.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲawvo_5037">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲawvo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲaw</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲawnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲawvo_5037_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>maigrir, dépérir, s'épuiser ; (nom) dépérissement, consomption</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>waste away, grow thin; (noun) wasting, emaciation</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.6 Symptom of disease"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.4.2 Weak"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 11 occurrences, first GEN.47.13; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲawvo; Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲàùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>vanndacieea kandu ɲawvo a yiaan « les gens dépérissaient de faim » (GEN.47.13).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲáŋáá_5038">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáŋáá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáŋgáá</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲáŋáá_5038_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce d'arbre (dur à casser)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind of tree (hard to break)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 274: ɲáŋáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲàŋàfòó_5039">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲàŋàfòó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲàŋgàfòó</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲàŋàfòó_5039_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>maladie qui provoque des démangeaisons</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>disease causing itching</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲàŋàfòó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲáŋgbáá_5040">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáŋgbáá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáŋmgbáá</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲáŋgbáá_5040_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>masque (« diable ») visible de tous qui critique tout le monde ; nom générique des masques</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>mask ('bush devil') seen by all that criticizes everyone; general name for masks</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.2 Supernatural being"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.8 Religious things"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲáŋgbáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲáŋgóó_5041">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáŋgóó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲàŋgòó</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲáŋgóó_5041_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>purificateur, exorciste (qui purifie les gens et les lieux)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cleanser, exorcist (who purifies people and places)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.5 Practice religion"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.4 Miracle, supernatural power"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲáŋgóó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲáŋòŋ-ɲàŋòŋ_5042">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáŋòŋ-ɲàŋòŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲáŋòŋ-ɲàŋòŋ_5042_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(marcher) à grands pas puissants, comme un géant</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(walk) powerfully, striding like a giant</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.1 Manner of movement"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲáŋòŋ-ɲàŋòŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲáɲáá_5043">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáɲáá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáɲáláŋ</text></form></field>
    <sense id="ɲáɲáá_5043_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>herbe basse à fleurs jaunes (arrête les saignements)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>low grass with yellow flowers (used to stanch bleeding)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.3 Grass, herb, vine"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.7 Treat disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲáɲáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲáɲáléŋ_5044">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲáɲáléŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲáɲáléŋ_5044_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce de plante (qui démange)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>kind of plant (causes itching)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5 Plant"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲáɲáléŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲeenun_5045">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲeenun</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲeenun_5045_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>reculer devant, fuir devant ; s'échapper</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shrink back from, flee from; escape</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.2.3 Move toward something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>run away from (benefactive of 'run')</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first 1SA.19.11; Childs 2000, p. 275: ɲèènɔ̌ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲéŋíó_5046">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲéŋíó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲéŋíó_5046_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>engourdissement, somnolence ; maladie du sommeil, tétanos ; venin</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>numbness, sleepiness; sleeping sickness, tetanus; venom</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.6 Symptom of disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 278: ɲéŋíó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲia_5047">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲia</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲia_5047_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>faveur (ca … ɲia « regarder avec faveur »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>favour (ca … ɲia 'look on with favour')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.4 Do good to"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 64 occurrences, first GEN.6.8</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲia kiyɛiya_5048">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲia kiyɛiya</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="ɲia kiyɛiya_5048_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>êtres vivants ; vers</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>living beings; worms</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.4 Living things"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲia kiyɛiya</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>ɲia et kiyɛiya sont dans la Bible séparément, pas l'expression.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲìàá_5049">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲìàá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲìàá_5049_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>aimer, chérir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>like, love</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.3 Love"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.1 Feel good"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 279: ɲìàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. peut-être ɲia « faveur » (Bible).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲifilaa_5050">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲifilaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲifila</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲifilaa_5050_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>plisser, froncer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wrinkle, frown</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.1 Shape"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲifilaa/ ɲifila</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le radical est glosé « passer, foncer » (pour « plisser, froncer » ?).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲìfìlɛ́-_5051">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲìfìlɛ́-</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲìfìlɛ́-_5051_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>ratatiné, tout petit</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>shrivelled up, very small</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.2.1 Small"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 279: ɲìfìlɛ́-</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲììmbúínáá_5052">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲììmbúínáá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲììmbúínáá_5052_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>très peu</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>very little</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.1 Quantity"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 279: ɲììmbúínáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲiimu-ɲiimu_5053">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲiimu-ɲiimu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲiimu-ɲiimoo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲiimu-ɲiimu_5053_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Ideophone"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>(idéophone) en chuchotant, à voix basse ; murmure</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>(ideophone) in a whisper, in a low voice; whispering</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="9.2.8 Ideophones"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first ISA.29.4; Childs 2000, p. 279: ɲíímú-ɲììmù</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲiinduuo_5054">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲiinduuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲiinduu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲiinduuo_5054_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>accuser (faussement) ; précipiter, pousser (en bas)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>accuse (falsely); push down, hurl down</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.7.5 Trial"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 4 occurrences, first 1KI.21.13; Childs 2000, p. 279: ɲììndùùwó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de ɲindu « pousser ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲiiyaa_5055">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲiiyaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲiiya</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲiiyanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲiiyaa_5055_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>trembler ; agiter</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>tremble, shake</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>shiver (from cold or fever); be anxious</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 56 occurrences, first JDG.5.5; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲiiyaa/ ɲiya; Childs 2000, p. 279: ɲììyáá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲììyàá-dìàlóŋ_5056">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲììyàá-dìàlóŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="ŋ"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲììyàá-dìàlóŋ_5056_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tremblements du corps ; paludisme</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>body trembling, shaking; malaria</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.2 Disease"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.6 Symptom of disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 280: ɲììyàá-dìàlóŋ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Cf. ɲiiyaa « trembler » (Bible).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲííye_5057">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲííye</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲííye_5057_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pitié, compassion</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>pity, compassion</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.4 Do good to"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4 Emotion"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>sorrow, pity, mercy</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 90 occurrences, first EXO.2.6; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲiiye; Childs 2000, p. 277: ɲɛ̀éyé</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>ɲííye bii X « X a pitié ». Lexique kissi–français, p. 39 : aussi ɲiye « la pitié, miséricorde ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲílífɔ̀ŋndó_5058">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲílífɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲílífɔ̀ŋndó_5058_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>uniforme</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>uniform</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.3 Clothing"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 280: ɲílífɔ̀ŋndó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Emprunt à l'anglais uniform.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲin_5059">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲin</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <sense id="ɲin_5059_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>temps, jour, moment</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>time, day, moment</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4 Time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲin</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La Bible a ɲin (1SA.1.26, 2SA.10.3), sens à vérifier.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲinaa_5060">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲinaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲinaa_5060_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>esprit, démon</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>spirit, demon</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.2 Supernatural being"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>spirit, esp. spirits of the land or of ancestors</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 120 occurrences, first DEU.18.11; Childs 2000, p. 280: ɲínàá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Invariable : ɲinaa vɔɔnda « les esprits mauvais ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲinasian_5061">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲinasian</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲinasian_5061_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>l'année prochaine</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>next year</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.1 Period of time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first 1KI.20.22; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲinasan</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique écrit ɲinasan (sans le i après s) ; ɲinasan lekɔɔli « après l'année prochaine » (Lexique, p. 39). Bible : telen vaa nuaa ɲinasian « l'année prochaine à cette époque » (1KI.20.22).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲinasiaŋ_5062">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲinasiaŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲinasian</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲinasiaŋ_5062_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adverb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>l'an prochain, à pareille époque l'an prochain</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>next year, at this time next year</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.5 Relative time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first GEN.17.21</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲindin_5063">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲindin</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="ɲindin_5063_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>appliquer (un remède) sur le corps ; mettre une compresse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>apply (a remedy) to the body; apply a compress</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.7 Treat disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 162: nyindin; Childs 2000, p. 280: ɲìndìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Keita (p. 162, dialogue sur un remède) : « a nyindin dialon a man ». Kissi du Sud ɲìndìó (Childs).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲindu_5064">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲindu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲindu_5064_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pousser, bousculer</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>push, press hard</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 31 occurrences, first GEN.19.9; Childs 2000, p. 280: ɲìndɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲindɔɔ_5065">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲindɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲindu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲindɔɔ_5065_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pousser, croître (feuilles, dents, cheveux) ; pousse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>grow, sprout (leaves, teeth, hair); shoot</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.6 Growth of plants"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲindɔɔ/ ɲindu</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Homographe de ɲindɔɔ/ ɲindu « pousser, bousculer » (Bible).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲirio_5066">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲirio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="ɲirio_5066_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>moucherons</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>gnats, midges</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲirio</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲìsɔ̀ɔ́_5067">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲìsɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲìsɔ̀ɔ́_5067_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se moucher</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>blow (one's nose)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.2.4 Mucus"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 280: ɲìsɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲjàkámɛ̀íyó_5068">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲjàkámɛ̀íyó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲjàkámɛ̀íyó_5068_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>aide à la moisson du riz (payée en nature)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>helping to harvest rice (paid with a share)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.2.5 Harvest"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="6.1 Work"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 283: ɲjàkámɛ̀íyó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲjélínɔ̀ɔ́_5069">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲjélínɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲjélíá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="ɲjélínɔ̀ɔ́_5069_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>interprète, voix du masque (esprit)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>interpreter, voice of the masked spirit</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.9.2 Supernatural being"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.9 Culture"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 284: ɲjélínɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲjòŋnìá_5070">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲjòŋnìá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲjòŋnìá_5070_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'accroupir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>squat</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.1 Posture"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 283: ɲjòŋnìá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲulu_5071">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲulu</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲulu_5071_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>paix, sécurité</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>peace, safety</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.4 Peace"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 57 occurrences, first GEN.49.21</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>nila ɲulu « en sécurité ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲuluan_5072">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuluan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuluma</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuluei</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲuluan_5072_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Adjective"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>frais, froid</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cool, cold</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.4 Hot"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 3 occurrences, first PRO.25.25; Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲùlú-</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>mɛmma ɲuluan « eau fraîche » (MAT.10.42, PRO.25.25) ; mɛmma ɲuluma (JER.18.14) ; ɲuluei (PRO.25.13, fraîcheur de la neige).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲùlùáŋ_5073">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲùlùáŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="ma"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲùlùáŋ_5073_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>potion, remède (eau froide mêlée de feuilles)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>potion, medicine (cold water mixed with leaves)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.7 Treat disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲùlùáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲulul_5074">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲulul</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲulul_5074_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se calmer, s'apaiser (kɔl)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>calm down, be appeased (kɔl)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.1 Feel good"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.8.4 Peace"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 47 occurrences, first GEN.27.44</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲulullo_5075">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲulullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲulullo_5075_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>froid ; se refroidir, se rafraîchir ; (kɔllo ɲulullo) être apaisé</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>cold; grow cold, cool down; (kɔllo ɲulullo) be soothed</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.4 Hot"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 5 occurrences, first 1SA.16.23; Lexique kissi–français, p. 40: ɲurullo</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique écrit ɲurullo « froid ». Bible : paalen … ɲɔɔ kandu ɲulullo « quand le jour fraîchit » (SNG.4.6) ; Saul … kɔllo ɲulullo « Saul était soulagé » (1SA.16.23). Comparer ɲuluan « frais, froid ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲúmbàltéŋ_5076">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲúmbàltéŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="le"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲúmbàltéŋ_5076_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>espèce d'arbre (sert à faire des pièges à rats)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>a tree species (used for rat traps)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.1 Tree"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲúmbàltéŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲúmbùláá_5077">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲúmbùláá</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲúmbùláá_5077_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>pénis non circoncis</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>uncircumcised penis</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.1.2 Torso"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲúmbùláá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumbɔɔ_5078">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumbɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuumbun</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲumbɔɔ_5078_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tourner (la meule), moudre ; (ɲuumbun) tourner (sur ses gonds)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>turn (a millstone), grind; (ɲuumbun) turn (on its hinges)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.2 Move something in a direction"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.1 Food preparation"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>twist, turn, braid</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 1 occurrences, first JDG.16.21; Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲùmbɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>pow bɛndu cuiyaa n'kullo ɲumbɔɔ « tourner la grosse meule » (JDG.16.21) ; mɛɛ dioo ɲuumbun o boondun ndɔn coo « comme la porte tourne sur ses gonds » (PRO.26.14).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumbɔɔ_5079">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumbɔɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="check"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumbu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲumbɔɔ_5079_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>tordre, entortiller, enrouler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>twist, wind, coil</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.4 Handle something"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲunbɔɔ/ ɲunbu</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Le Lexique écrit ɲunbɔɔ/ ɲunbu ; la Bible n'écrit jamais nb. La Bible a ɲumbɔɔ une fois, en parlant de Samson qui tourne la meule (kullo ɲumbɔɔ, JDG.16.21) ; sens à vérifier.</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumi_5080">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumi</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲumi_5080_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>effacer, anéantir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wipe out, blot out</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.9.3 Destroy"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 39 occurrences, first EXO.32.32</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲùmícílìó_5081">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲùmícílìó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <field type="plural"><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲùmícílìá</text></form></field>
    <sense id="ɲùmícílìó_5081_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>luciole</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>firefly</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲùmícílìó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumio_5082">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumio</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumi</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲumio_5082_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>éteindre (le feu)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>extinguish, quench (fire)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>extinguish, put out (causative of 'go out')</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 7 occurrences, first PSA.9.6; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲumio/ ɲumi; Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲùmìó</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Causatif de ɲumndo « s'éteindre » ; même forme que ɲumi « effacer, anéantir ». Vana-vana venin le yinnde len ɲumio le « personne ne l'éteindra » (ISA.1.31, AMO.5.6, JER.21.12) ; kɔɔn … kpow ɲumio « éteindre toutes les flèches enflammées » (EPH.6.16).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumndan_5083">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumndan</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲumndan_5083_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>obscurité ; nuit</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>darkness; night</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 179 occurrences, first GEN.1.4; Keita 1979, p. 154: Nyumndan; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲumndan; Childs 2000, p. 282: ɲùmndáŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumndo_5084">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumndo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲum</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumnin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲumndo_5084_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>s'éteindre ; pâlir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>go out (fire, lamp); fade</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.5 Fire"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.3.3 Light"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 15 occurrences, first LEV.13.6; Childs 2000, p. 283: ɲùmndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumullo_5085">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumullo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="ɲumullo_5085_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>démanger</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>itch, be itchy</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.3.5 Sense of touch"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="2.5.6 Symptom of disease"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲumullo; Childs 2000, p. 283: ɲùmùlló</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Confirmé au Nord par le Lexique kissi–français, p. 39 (« démangeaison »).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲúmúlúŋ-tùmndóŋ_5086">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲúmúlúŋ-tùmndóŋ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲúmúlúŋ-tùmndóŋ_5086_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>nourriture, riz cuit (argot ; litt. « anus qui démange »)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>food, cooked rice (slang; lit. 'itchy anus')</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="5.2.3 Types of food"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 283: ɲúmúlúŋ-tùmndóŋ</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲumɛiyo_5087">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲumɛiyo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="ɲumɛiyo_5087_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>vendredi</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>Friday</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4.4 Telling time"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Keita 1979, p. 152: Nyumèiyo; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲumɛiyo</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲunaa_5088">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲunaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuna</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲunanin</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲunan</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲunaa_5088_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>demander, interroger</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ask, question</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.2 Request"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>ask; beg for</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 106 occurrences, first JDG.11.12; Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲunaa/ ɲuna; Childs 2000, p. 283: ɲùnàá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲuniaa_5089">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuniaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲunia</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲuniaa_5089_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>demander plusieurs fois</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>ask repeatedly</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.2 Request"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 40: ɲuniaa/ ɲunia</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Pluriel de ɲunaa « demander ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲuuniaa_5090">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuuniaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuunianndo</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲuuniaa_5090_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>interroger (en détail), questionner</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>question closely, interrogate</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.5.1 Say"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>plural of 'ask'</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 31 occurrences, first GEN.43.7; Childs 2000, p. 283: ɲùùnìá</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Dérivé de ɲunaa « demander ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲuuo_5091">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuuo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲuu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲuuo_5091_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>avoir du dégoût pour qqn, détourner la tête de dégoût</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>feel disgust for someone, turn one's head away in disgust</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.4.2 Feel bad"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 40: ɲuuo/ ɲuu</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲɔ_5092">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔ</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="respelled"/>
    <sense id="ɲɔ_5092_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>temps (qu'il fait ?)</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>time; weather (?)</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="8.4 Time"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.1.3 Weather"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Lexique kissi–français, p. 39: ɲɔ</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>Voir aussi ɲɛmu-ɲɛmu ɲɔ « brouillard ».</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲɔfɔliaa_5093">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔfɔliaa</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔfɔla</text></form></variant>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔfɔliaanin</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲɔfɔliaa_5093_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>se faner, se flétrir</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>wither, fade</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.5.6 Growth of plants"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 10 occurrences, first 1KI.8.37</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>ɲɔfɔlɛiya « flétris » (ISA.64.5).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲɔ̀kɔ̀tɔ́ŋndó_5094">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔ̀kɔ̀tɔ́ŋndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔ́kɔ́tɔ́ŋndó</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲɔ̀kɔ̀tɔ́ŋndó_5094_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>instrument à cordes avec un bâton fixé sur une calebasse</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>stringed instrument with a stick attached to a gourd</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.2.3 Music"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 280: ɲɔ̀kɔ̀tɔ́ŋndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲɔla_5095">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔla</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <sense id="ɲɔla_5095_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>prendre une poignée de, puiser à pleine main</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>take a handful of, scoop up</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="7.3.4 Handle something"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>pinch; give someone a small portion</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 6 occurrences, first GEN.2.7; Childs 2000, p. 281: ɲɔ̀làá</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲɔ́mndó_5096">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔ́mndó</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="noun-class" value="o"/>
    <trait name="status" value="southern"/>
    <sense id="ɲɔ́mndó_5096_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Noun"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>grand animal apparenté au singe</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>large animal related to the monkey</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="1.6.1 Types of animals"/>
    </sense>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>Childs 2000, p. 281: ɲɔ́mndó</text></form></note>
  </entry>
  <entry id="ɲɔɔloo_5097">
    <lexical-unit><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔɔloo</text></form></lexical-unit>
    <trait name="status" value="attested"/>
    <variant><form lang="kqs"><text>ɲɔɔlu</text></form></variant>
    <sense id="ɲɔɔloo_5097_s1">
      <grammatical-info value="Verb"/>
      <gloss lang="fr"><text>supplier ; consoler</text></gloss>
      <gloss lang="en"><text>beg, entreat; comfort</text></gloss>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="3.3.2 Request"/>
      <trait name="semantic-domain-ddp4" value="4.3.4 Do good to"/>
    </sense>
    <field type="southern-kissi-sense"><form lang="en"><text>beg, beseech, ask forgiveness</text></form></field>
    <note type="source"><form lang="en"><text>BKG: 40 occurrences, first GEN.24.67; Childs 2000, p. 281: ɲɔ̀ɔ̀lɔ̀ɔ́</text></form></note>
    <note><form lang="fr"><text>La forme longue sert aussi de nom : « consolation » (Gn 24,67).</text></form></note>
  </entry>
